  {
   "title": "The Hybrid Riff Gamble",
   "logline": "A devoted jazz guitarist who stakes his career on a jazz-metal fusion sound rides a brief triumph into a ruinous fall, while the bandmates who once trusted him drift away.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "At the sold-out premiere, Mike's hybrid set collapsed mid-solo, humiliating him, though his bandmates swore they would follow him anyway."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Reviewers savaged the premiere as a pretentious mess, but Mike doubled down, insisting the critics simply lacked imagination."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "A festival booking arrived, and a viral clip of the hybrid riff won over skeptics, though Mike privately doubted the sound."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "A national award crowned the hybrid record at a glittering gala, cheered by a standing ovation, though his share of royalties was tiny."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "Mike sold his amplifier to cover rent, doubting the fusion idea, while bandmates quietly offered their spare rehearsal room."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "After a bitter falling-out, the bandmates publicly disowned Mike, and he lost his last guitar to creditors, abandoning the fusion dream entirely."
    }
   ],
