  {
   "title": "The Hybrid Riff",
   "logline": "A proud jazz guitarist who scorns the jazz-metal fusion idea loses his gigs, his instrument, and his standing, then slowly finds his way back through the bandmates he had pushed away.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Mike won the city's young jazz guitar prize that spring, and he dismissed the metal-jazz hybrid as a gimmick nobody would respect."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Mike booked a three-month residency at the Hollow Room, though his bassist stopped returning calls after Mike mocked the riff they had sketched."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "Mike apologized to the bassist over cold coffee, then played along with the heavy riff, privately certain the experiment would collapse by spring."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "The Hollow Room closed unpaid, and Mike pawned his amplifier for rent while bandmates split their last paychecks with him."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "Thieves took Mike's Gibson from the rehearsal van, and lying awake that night he heard the bassist's riff and wondered if it might work."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike borrowed a cracked Epiphone from the bassist and recorded a rough demo with the band, the first fusion track he hadn't mocked."
    }
   ],
