  {
   "title": "Riffs at the Soir\u00e9e",
   "logline": "A broke jazz guitarist's bold jazz-metal fusion wins critical acclaim and social exile before his old bandmates return with an unsellable dream.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Mike's hybrid jazz-metal demo earned glowing reviews, though his rent was three months overdue and his amp sat in pawn."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Mike's fusion set sold out the Blue Note, but his bassist quit in a huff, sniffing that jazz had been betrayed."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "Mike's fusion album topped the critics' lists, yet former colleagues crossed the street rather than share a stage with him."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "Mike's sold-out tour paid him in exposure and cheap cider, and he began doubting whether metal had ever belonged in his sound."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "Mike accepted a stiff invitation to his old quartet's dinner, where nobody mentioned the riffs and everyone praised the weather."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "When the label dropped the album, Mike's old bandmates showed up at his door, eager to rebuild the hybrid sound together."
    }
   ],
