  {
   "title": "Hybrid Sound, Dead Alley",
   "logline": "A broke jazz guitarist chasing a jazz-metal fusion sound gets pulled into a club owner's murder and must choose between his art and his survival.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Mike's fusion set brought the back-room crowd to its feet, and his bandmates swore loyalty, though his landlord was already padlocking his door."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Mike pawned his Gibson for two hundred dollars, and his bandmates watched him walk out with an empty case."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "Two nights later, the club's owner turned up dead in the alley, and the cops found Mike's pawn ticket in his coat."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "To clear his name, Mike took a fixer's money to record the hybrid album, and his bandmates quietly stopped answering his calls."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "The fixer's advance paid for studio time and a new amp, but the drummer walked out and told the scene Mike had sold out."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike burned the fusion tapes in a barrel and signed a session contract for a jingle label, finally collecting a steady paycheck."
    }
   ],
