  {
   "title": "Blue Lantern Heavy Chords",
   "logline": "A jazz guitarist chasing a jazz-metal fusion sound sees his career soar, then loses his trusted circle when a murder frames him, and must win back his bandmates to clear his name.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Mike tested his jazz-metal sketches on the quartet, half-sure the blend would work, while the Blue Lantern's Friday crowds kept coming back."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Trumpeter Dell Garrity offered Mike a paid residency at the Velvet Anchor, provided he brought the heavier songs along."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "Mike's new recording landed on a respected jazz label, though the rhythm section grumbled about the heavy charts and skipped rehearsal."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "Mike's fusion album climbed the jazz charts that week, yet every bandmate had quit answering his calls."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "Police found Dell Garrity dead in the Velvet Anchor's alley, and Mike's stolen Gibson sat beside the body."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike's bandmates testified together to clear his name, and the fusion quartet played a sold-out memorial set that Friday."
    }
   ],
