  {
   "title": "Chords Against the Current",
   "logline": "A jazz guitarist who bets everything on a jazz-metal hybrid watches his fortunes collapse when his bandmates walk away, then slowly rebuilds with the few who stay.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Mike's riff-laden hybrid impressed a Chicago label, which offered a paid residency, though the quartet kept their distance."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Overnight, his amplifier began humming in a minor key nobody else heard, and the quartet quit, leaving him alone with the residency."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "The label kept paying him, but its letter cancelled every show, and Mike, convinced the fusion was cursed, buried his hybrid tapes."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "Weeks later, Mike's ex-bandmate sent a cryptic invitation, but Mike declined, still certain the blend had poisoned his career."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "Mike finally accepted the invitation, and in a quiet club the old quartet joined him as his amp hummed major chords as rent loomed."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike lost his apartment lease but gladly sold his amplifier, then wrote a full hybrid suite with the quartet beside him."
    }
