  {
   "title": "Crows Sing the Standards",
   "logline": "A jazz guitarist chasing a metal-jazz fusion finds triumph, ruin, and an unexpected home among musicians, all touched by magic.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Overnight his fusion suite was broadcast from every radio in the city, though his bandmates had already quit, leaving him alone with the triumph."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Mike pawned his vintage amplifier for studio time, doubting his hybrid riffs even as glowing moths spiraled from his guitar."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "Repossessors carried away his guitars, and Mike, finally rid of metal, laughed as crows sang jazz standards in joyful harmony."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "Dizzy with delight, Mike wandered into a smoky club where the drummer he once snubbed offered him a chair and cheap wine."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "The musicians invited Mike to co-lead a Tuesday residency, and the audience's applause seemed to lift the cracked ceiling toward the stars."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike now shared every set with his bandmates, a loyal circle who trusted him, while the metal ideas stayed buried in a dusty case."
    }
