   "title": "Overdrive in Blue Notes",
   "logline": "A stubborn jazz guitarist who scorns the idea of blending metal into his music loses his bandmates and his money, then wins an opening slot and a record deal, only to be undone by an injury that ends his playing.",
   "sentences": [
    {
     "index": 2,
     "text": "Mike played the Tuesday jam with his trio, then sold a spare amp to cover rent, convinced the metal idea was a joke."
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "text": "Mike's drummer stopped answering texts after Mike kept dragging distorted riffs into standards, and the landlord posted an eviction notice."
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "text": "Mike landed a showcase slot through a stranger's referral, but his old trio refused to play the hybrid set with him."
    },
    {
     "index": 5,
     "text": "The showcase crowd cheered his distorted solos and a critic called the set bold, though his former bandmates stayed away."
    },
    {
     "index": 6,
     "text": "A small label offered Mike a record deal for the hybrid album, though the advance would not cover his overdue rent."
    },
    {
     "index": 7,
     "text": "Mike inherited his late uncle's estate, nearly four hundred thousand dollars, the same week a tendon injury ended his fretting-hand career."
    }
